        "body": "## Problem\n\nThe verification and publish steps are disconnected in the UI:\n\n1. **Quick Connect** (Step 2) verifies via OAuth but stores no session state about what was verified. The success banner is transient. As of `ff2697d`, the Advanced section auto-opens with the publish button visible after OAuth, but this only works for the single most recent verification.\n\n2. **Proof-post** (Step 3) has a publish button, but it only publishes the currently selected platform/identity from the form fields. There's no way to verify multiple platforms and publish them together.\n\n3. **Each publish is a full kind 0 replacement.** Verifying Twitter then publishing, then verifying Bluesky then publishing, means two kind 0 sign-and-broadcast cycles. The second one could race with the first if relays are slow.\n\n4. **No session state** tracks what's been verified. Refreshing the page loses all context about completed verifications.\n\n## Proposal\n\nAdd a **Verified Links** panel between Step 2 and Step 3 (hidden until first verification). It tracks all successful verifications in the current session and provides individual and batch publish.\n\n### UI\n\n```\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────\nYour Verified Links\n\n  ✅ bluesky: machination.org     [Publish]  [×]\n  ✅ twitter: mjb                  [Publish]  [×]\n\n  [Publish All to Nostr Profile]\n\n  Publish writes identity tags into your signed Nostr profile (kind 0).\n  \"Publish All\" adds all verified links in a single update.\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n```\n\n### Behavior\n\n- **Session-level `verifiedLinks` array** stores `{platform, identity, proof}` for each successful verification (OAuth or proof-post).\n- **OAuth callback** pushes to `verifiedLinks` and renders the panel.\n- **Proof-post success** pushes to `verifiedLinks` and renders the panel.\n- **Individual Publish** works like today: fetches kind 0, updates one `i` tag, signs, publishes.\n- **Publish All** fetches kind 0 once, adds/updates all `i` tags from `verifiedLinks`, signs once, publishes once. One signature prompt, one relay broadcast. This is the main UX win.\n- **Remove (×)** removes from session list (doesn't revoke verification).\n- **Panel hidden** when `verifiedLinks` is empty.\n\n### Cycle\n\nThe intended user flow becomes:\n\n```\nLog in (Step 1)\n  ↓\nVerify platform A (Quick Connect or proof-post)\n  ↓\nVerify platform B (Quick Connect or proof-post)\n  ↓\n... repeat as needed ...\n  ↓\nReview Verified Links panel\n  ↓\nPublish All → single kind 0 update with all identity tags\n```\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- `verifiedLinks` is in-memory only (no persistence needed beyond the session)\n- The panel replaces the current pattern of the publish button living inside the Advanced section\n- Keep the existing Advanced publish button for backward compatibility (or remove it if the panel fully replaces the need)\n- `publishIdentityTagToNostr()` already handles tag deduplication (line 1784) so it's safe to publish tags that already exist in the profile\n\n### Context\n\nNear-term fix shipped in `ff2697d`: after OAuth callback, pre-fill the Advanced form and open the section so the publish button is reachable. This is a workaround. The verified links panel is the proper solution.",
